WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.344
Four forces run the entire universe.

2
00:00:03.444 --> 00:00:05.105
Let's watch each one at work.

3
00:00:09.799 --> 00:00:16.062
Everything that happens, from a falling apple to a shining star, comes down to just four forces.

4
00:00:16.663 --> 00:00:25.269
The strong force glues quarks together. Pull on one, and the force stays the same however far you stretch it: about 16 tonnes.

5
00:00:25.368 --> 00:00:28.196
Until the string snaps into brand-new particles.

6
00:00:28.996 --> 00:00:38.893
Between protons, a leftover of the strong force holds the nucleus together. Switch it off, and the protons' own electric repulsion blows it apart.

7
00:00:40.292 --> 00:00:48.281
Electromagnetism acts on charge. Halve the distance between two charges, and the force becomes four times stronger.

8
00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:56.939
Shake a charge, and ripples spread out at the speed of light. That ripple is light itself, from radio waves to violet.

9
00:00:58.138 --> 00:01:07.368
The weak force can change one kind of quark into another. A neutron's down quark becomes an up quark, throwing out an electron and an antineutrino.

10
00:01:08.969 --> 00:01:14.587
That slow, rare process powers the Sun, and sends floods of neutrinos straight through the Earth.

11
00:01:15.787 --> 00:01:24.293
Gravity curves space itself. Launch too slowly and you fall in. Just right, and you orbit forever. Too fast, and you escape.

12
00:01:26.692 --> 00:01:33.236
Yet gravity is by far the weakest force. A tiny fridge magnet beats the pull of the entire planet.

13
00:01:36.766 --> 00:01:38.979
The strong force holds atoms together.

14
00:01:39.079 --> 00:01:41.954
Electromagnetism builds chemistry and light.

15
00:01:42.054 --> 00:01:45.335
And gravity is the weakest, yet it shapes the cosmos.

16
00:01:44.166 --> 00:01:46.225
Next time: states of matter.
